From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 17:07:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] gluon-mesh-batman-adv: announce the link MTU in router
 advertisements

Our clients reach everything through a tunnel whose MTU is well below
the 1500 bytes they assume on br-client, and they only find out about it
from the ICMP errors that come back -- when they come back.

Pass the MTU on to them (RFC 4861) when noderoute has written it to
/tmp/adv_mtu, the same way the NAT64 prefix is passed on. --adv-link-mtu
needs uradvd from the freifunkMUC fork (pinned by site-ffm at 780182a),
and one built without it exits before sending a single advertisement, so
the option only appears when a node has told us what to advertise.

uradvd refuses a link MTU below the 1280 bytes IPv6 needs; noderoute
does not write the file in that case, rather than have it die on the
argument.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../luasrc/lib/gluon/radvd/arguments                      | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/package/gluon-mesh-batman-adv/luasrc/lib/gluon/radvd/arguments b/package/gluon-mesh-batman-adv/luasrc/lib/gluon/radvd/arguments
index 1fae015e..9052b35c 100755
--- a/package/gluon-mesh-batman-adv/luasrc/lib/gluon/radvd/arguments
+++ b/package/gluon-mesh-batman-adv/luasrc/lib/gluon/radvd/arguments
@@ -23,6 +23,14 @@ if pref64 then
 	io.write(" --pref64 " .. pref64)
 end
 
+-- Everything our clients send leaves through a tunnel, so they are told
+-- what fits into it (RFC 4861). noderoute writes the file while that is
+-- known, and never writes a value uradvd would refuse to advertise.
+local adv_mtu = util.readfile("/tmp/adv_mtu")
+if adv_mtu then
+	io.write(" --adv-link-mtu " .. adv_mtu)
+end
+
 if site.radvd() then
 	if site.radvd.preferred_lifetime() then
 		io.write(" --preferred-lifetime " .. site.radvd.preferred_lifetime())
-- 
